{%- comment -%}
  PG Hero Crop: shorten the first gallery image on the Crystal PokeOrb page.

  The orb hero is a near-square studio shot whose bottom third is nothing but
  the mirrored reflection of the five orbs on the black tabletop. It carries no
  product information, and it pushes the buy column's opening content that much
  further down the page.

  The box is cropped to 16:10, which lands just under the bases -- the product
  is untouched, only the reflection is trimmed. object-position is top so the
  crop always comes off the bottom rather than being centred.

  pg-landing does this same trick inline for the wall art template, whose room
  shot has a lot of empty bedding under the print. It lives in its own section
  here rather than being added there because pg-landing is a 35KB shared file
  and a themeFilesUpsert rewrites the whole thing.

  DESKTOP ONLY, deliberately. pg-gallery-mobile sets these images to
  aspect-ratio:auto with object-fit:contain, which is what stopped the mobile
  hero being cropped into a square -- a problem that was reported and fixed.
  Cropping at narrow widths would walk straight back into it, so the rule is
  gated above the 900px breakpoint pg-landing already uses to switch layouts.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if template.suffix == 'pg-crystal' -%}
<style>
  @media (min-width: 901px){
    html body #pgx .pgx-hero img{
      aspect-ratio:16/10 !important;
      object-fit:cover !important;
      object-position:center top !important;
      width:100% !important;
      height:auto !important;
    }
  }
</style>
{%- endif -%}
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Hero Crop", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
